---
# The pilot mTLS policy: the SSO path.
#
# Keycloak is the estate's single-consumer SSO gateway and its only
# east-west dependency is its own database (keycloak-db, port 5432). That
# makes it the cleanest pair to enforce mutual authentication on: no
# shared provider, no shared consumer, so requiring mTLS on this one flow
# cannot black-hole anything else, and a broken rule is visible as the SSO
# path, not as a cascade. It is the pilot per the plan's D2 (the final
# per-service list is owned by the implement task and expands from here).
#
# What this enforces: a connection entering keycloak-db from keycloak on
# 5432/TCP must complete an out-of-band mTLS handshake between the two
# Cilium agents (port 4250, backed by SPIRE SVIDs) before it is admitted.
# The mTLS requirement attaches to the receiving side (the database's
# ingress), which is the enforcement point - the sender needs no policy of
# its own. Because the chart runs with enableNonDefaultDenyPolicies: false,
# this rule is purely additive: it adds mTLS to this one flow and leaves
# every other flow into keycloak-db default-allow. Removing this file
# (via Flux prune) restores default-allow on 5432 and drops mTLS, the
# pre-feature baseline.
#
# Nothing here touches Traefik or the platform Gateway: they keep
# terminating TLS at the edge and simply ride the now-encrypted pod
# network as ordinary endpoints.
apiVersion: cilium.io/v2
kind: CiliumNetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: cnp-mutual-auth-keycloak-db
  namespace: keycloak
spec:
  endpointSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: keycloak-db
  ingress:
    - fromEndpoints:
        - matchLabels:
            app: keycloak
      authentication:
        mode: "required"
      toPorts:
        - ports:
            - port: "5432"
              protocol: TCP
